title: Right on Cue
id: right-on-cue
tab: Neon & Cue · Right on Cue
about: Cue has a mark but no line. Neon has a tune and nowhere to stand.
lead: scribe
key: D mixolydian
bpm: 112
backing:
bass: none
stage: vee, scribe
finale: "Cue" on 0

[the offer]
scribe: "I've got a mark" = 0/.5 2/.5 4 2/2 | I 4
vee: "I've got a tune" = -3/.75 -2/.25 0 2/2 | I 4
scribe: "I've lost my line" = 1/.5 3/.5 5 3/2 | IV 4
vee: "Then borrow two" = 2/.75 3/.25 4 6/2 | VII 4

[step inside]
scribe: "I lay the loop" = 0 2/.5 3/.5 4/2 | I 4
vee: "I step inside" = 4 5/.5 4/.5 2/2 | IV 4
scribe: "Your turn to shine" = 1 3/.5 2/.5 1/2 | V 4
vee: "Your turn to try" = -3 0 2 4 | I 4

[right on cue]
scribe: "Right on cue" = 4/.75 3/.25 2/3 | I 4
  + vee: "One light" = 2 0/3
vee: "Right on cue" = 5/.75 4/.25 3/3 | IV 4
  + scribe: "One more" = 3 1/3
scribe: "One little loop makes room for two" = 0/.5 2/.5 4 4 3 2 1 0/2 | IV 4, I 4
  + vee: "Two lights one song" = 5/2 4/2 2/2 2/2

[missed entrance]
scribe: "And now we bow" = 2 3/.5 4/.5 1/2 | V 4
rest 2
vee: "Too soon" = 4/.5 2/1.5 | I 2
scribe: "I meant to do that" = 0/.5 0/.5 2 1 0 | I 4

[repeat right on cue]
